In compound houses, energy consumption tracking and accountability is paramount. Due to how important it has become
especially in this current data driven world, many researchers have come up with technologies like 
smart meters, Meter-Bus protocol(MBus) among others to make the collection of data from meters easy and 
seamless. Watcal project seeks to design a system that would make sharing of bills seamles and user intuitive
leveraging MBus and TCP/IP techologies to ensure that this goal is achieved at a minimal cost. Our goal
is to ensures that users get feedback on what they consume to enforce responsible energy consumption. Moreover, this 
project provides a accountability and peace coexistence among individuals in compound houses.
